Notebook[
 {Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["HEPCAT SYMBOL", "PacletNameCell"],
       Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["HEPCAT", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/HEPCAT"], "  \[Bullet]  ",
          ButtonBox["Related Guide", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/AmplitudeConstruction"]}],
        "AnchorBar"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Right}},
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.42], Scaled[0.58]}}]],
   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["PrepareAmplitudes", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Simplify diagram pairs or factorization rows while retaining their \
physical assumptions.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"PrepareAmplitudes", "[", "items", ",",
         " ", "model", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "Prepare a mass-rule \
pair, a list of diagram pairs or compact factorization-channel rows."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"PrepareAmplitudes", "[", "items", ",",
         " ", "model", ",", " ", "\"PolePreference\"", " ", "->", " ",
         "preference", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "Choose and simplify a \
bounded set of allowed reference-spinor assignments."}], "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"PrepareAmplitudes", "[", "items", ",",
         " ", "model", ",", " ", "\"ReturnDetails\"", " ", "->", " ", "True",
         "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "Retain original inputs, selected \
references, discarded remainders and preparation diagnostics."}], "Usage"],
  Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["The ordinary result retains the \
input format with each expression replaced by its prepared form. \"Output\" \
-> \"Expression\" returns the sum instead. The detailed report is optional so \
routine use does not expose implementation data.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Preparation applies ReduceSpinContractions, chooses reference \
spinors, then applies ReduceSpinorProducts and bounded improving identities. \
Momentum conservation is used with the known external leg set rather than \
added as an unconditional chain rewrite.", "Notes"],
  Cell["A bounded numerator pass can factor existing spectator spinor chains \
to expose small Schouten and external Dirac identities. Each complete \
inverse-factor product stays separate, inverse factors are protected, and \
only a strict improvement of the complete expression is retained. Unsupported \
sectors and interrupted trials keep their last completed expression.",
   "Notes"], Cell["A further bounded ordinary-identity pass handles supported \
numerators with six distinct external spinor slots and at most one momentum \
insertion per monomial. It searches Schouten, external Dirac and, when \
enabled, declared total-momentum-conservation identities. A numerical \
optimization only proposes a sparse form: exact rational identity \
coefficients and a zero algebraic replay residual are required before \
accepting it. Denominators and internal virtualities are unchanged; this does \
not prove a global minimum.", "Notes"], Cell["For completed external \
amplitudes, ordinary external pair definitions can first cancel apparent \
repeated propagators without internal-shell conditions. A bounded \
shared-matrix identity can then expose one or two literal positive spectator \
chain factors and smaller six-spinor coefficients. A two-factor route removes \
only witnessed polynomial factors, preserves each original fraction, and \
requires exact identity replay after lifting the spectators back. Inverse \
factors are unchanged by that cofactor route. Only complete improving \
checkpoints are returned. This final-amplitude route leaves the \
diagram/channel source partitions used by completion unchanged.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Constructive internal-shell simplification acts on each item's \
numerator using only that item's mass declarations. Physical PropDen objects \
stay off shell. A channel row declares only its own cut; completed \
external-mass pairs declare no internal cut.", "Notes"],
  Cell["ReduceSpinorProducts itself applies the ordinary external-shell \
identities. The additional diagram-local internal-shell reductions belong to \
preparation and may be disabled with \"InternalOnShell\" -> False.",
   "Notes"], Cell["\"PolePreference\" -> \"AllPhysical\" compares \
momentum-insertion references that introduce physical denominator channels \
outside the current diagram's cuts. \"AllSpurious\" compares references built \
from other eligible massless particles. \"Mixed\" permits both; Automatic \
compares admissible choices within a bounded budget.", "Notes"],
  Cell["\"Cyclic\" and \"ReverseCyclic\" retain fixed massless reference \
cycles. \"Xi\" uses a common reference, \"IndependentXi\" keeps separate \
generic references, and None leaves the references unchanged. An unavailable \
requested choice is reported rather than silently declared successful.",
   "Notes"], Cell["The search ranks completed trials by expression complexity \
and respects bounded time and candidate limits. Measuring a completed \
candidate has a separate bounded allowance from distributing identity trials, \
so a moderately large but cheaply measured expression is still ranked by its \
spinor complexity. A leaf-count fallback is not compared against a \
weighted-complexity score. The search does not prove a global minimum. \
Automatic resource settings scale to the process; user values remain \
authoritative.", "Notes"], Cell["The detailed output retains original \
expressions and discarded remainders so CompleteFactorization can first reuse \
information lost in aggressive preparation. Pass the report itself when \
preserving that information matters.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Feynman inputs use coherent external references for the whole diagram \
sum and never declare internal lines on shell. The reference assignment is \
fixed before independent items are sent to workers.", "Notes"],
  Cell["\"Parallelization\" and \"MaxKernels\" default to Automatic. Items \
are independent jobs, input order is retained, and user progress runs on the \
main kernel. \"MaxSteps\" -> 0 disables the bounded identity search but keeps \
deterministic algebraic and permitted scalar-shell reductions.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The same interface can simplify a completed amplitude returned as \
{externalMassRules, expression}; with no internal mass declarations it uses \
only ordinary identities. It never adds factorization corrections or model \
interactions.", "Notes"], Cell["Options", "NotesSection"],
  Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["Option", "TableHeader"],
       Cell["Default", "TableHeader"], Cell["Meaning", "TableHeader"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"PolePreference\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Reference and \
representation preference shared by preparation and completion. Automatic \
compares or inherits admissible choices; \"AllPhysical\", \"AllSpurious\" and \
\"Mixed\" bias pole forms, while cyclic/common/independent reference choices \
and None are also available. Required checks remain unchanged.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ExternalParticles\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Ordered external particle \
names when compact amplitude pairs no longer retain the process. Automatic \
uses recorded metadata or only unambiguous model matches; equal masses alone \
never establish identical species.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"FermionHelicities\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Leg-to-helicity rules or an association \
specifying massless Dirac external states for Feynman conversion. Required \
missing massless-fermion helicities are reported rather than guessed.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxReferenceChoices\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum reference \
assignments tried during bounded preparation. Automatic currently allows up \
to 64 trials, subject to the shared reference and item clocks; this is not \
exhaustive global minimization.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ReferenceTimeConstraint\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Budget for reference \
comparisons in checking, or reference-choice search in preparation. Automatic \
bounds this work; preparation shares it with the remaining per-item clock \
rather than adding an unlimited extra search.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"InternalOnShell\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether preparation may use declared constructive \
internal-channel masses in each item's numerator. True never puts PropDen \
denominators on shell and never transfers one diagram's assumptions to \
another; False leaves internal-shell reductions disabled.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxSteps\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum improving \
identity-search steps during preparation. Automatic scales the bounded effort \
to the workload; 0 retains deterministic contraction, spinor and permitted \
scalar-shell reductions while skipping the search.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxCandidates\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Bound on candidate \
identity edits considered during preparation. Automatic selects a finite \
workload-dependent allowance rather than searching every possible route.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"TimeConstraint\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum elapsed time \
allowed by the operation or stage. Where Automatic is supported it selects a \
finite workload-dependent budget; explicit seconds or supported Infinity \
override it. A timeout is reported, never treated as a successful amplitude."\
, "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MomentumConservation\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether identities may use the complete declared \
external momentum sum. The operation uses the known external-leg list rather \
than imposing unrelated internal cut conditions.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Parallelization\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether independent items \
or checks may use local Wolfram workers. Automatic uses suitable parallel \
work within available resources; False requests serial evaluation, and result \
order is retained.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxKernels\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum local Wolfram \
worker kernels available to parallel stages. Automatic respects processor \
availability and license limits; 1 requests serial execution. Worker setup \
and expression transfer can outweigh small jobs.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressReporting\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether preparation and construction stages \
display their progress. False suppresses the live stage display without \
changing the algebra or validation.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressFunction\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Optional callback \
receiving stage progress information. Automatic uses the normal progress \
display; callbacks are evaluated on the main kernel rather than independently \
by workers.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ReturnDetails\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether to expose optional diagnostic data \
instead of the compact default result. For preparation and factorization \
completion it retains provenance, directions and validation and takes \
precedence over Output; for export it returns file paths and build/run \
results.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Output\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Amplitudes\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Choose the amount and \
shape of returned information. Defaults are a compact check table, prepared \
input forms, a completed {externalMassRules, expression} pair, or a bare \
constructed expression; \"Details\" preserves diagnostics and provenance.",
        "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment ->
      {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Left}}, GridBoxItemSize ->
      {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.23], Scaled[0.19], Scaled[0.58]}},
     GridBoxDividers -> {"Rows" -> {False, True, {False}, False}}]],
   "3ColumnTableMod"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
the local HEPCAT checkout; no model parameters are assigned global numerical \
values.", "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"If", "[", "!", "StringQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", " ", "||", " ", "!", "DirectoryQ",
